        Root cause:
        The bug was likely caused by an incorrect handling of the scavenged static object list during garbage collection when multiple threads were involved. The original implementation assumed that the same logic could be applied regardless of the number of threads, which led to potential access violations or crashes when trying to zero out the static object lists for multiple threads simultaneously. The modification ensures that if there is only one thread, it directly accesses that thread's list, preventing issues that arise from iterating over potentially uninitialized or invalid thread references.

